 intro="After a tour of power sharing, federalism, social divisions and parties, this chapter asks a general question: what does democracy do, and does it fulfil our expectations? It assesses democracy under five heads: quality of government, economic well-being, inequality, social differences and conflict, and dignity and freedom.",
 big_questions=["How do we assess the outcomes of democracy?", "Does democracy give accountable, responsive and legitimate government?", "What is the record on growth and inequality?", "How does democracy handle social diversity, dignity and freedom?"],
