 ("h2", "1. How Do We Assess Democracy's Outcomes?"),
 ("p", "In Class IX students felt that democracy is better than dictatorship because it promotes equality among citizens, enhances the dignity of the individual, improves the quality of decision making, provides a method to resolve conflicts and allows room to correct mistakes. Most people support democracy against rule by a monarch, the military or religious leaders, yet few are satisfied with democracy in practice. Democracy is good in principle but felt to be not so good in practice."),
 ("p", "Over a hundred countries claim to be democratic: they have constitutions, elections, parties and guarantee rights. But they differ in social situation, economic achievement and culture, so what they achieve will differ. The first step is to recognise that **democracy is just a form of government**. It can only create conditions for achieving something; the citizens have to use those conditions."),
