 ("h2", "3. Economic Growth and Development"),
 ("p", "If democracies produce good government, is it fair to expect development? Evidence shows many democracies did not fulfil this expectation. Over the fifty years 1950-2000 dictatorships had a slightly higher rate of growth. But economic development depends on population size, global situation, cooperation from other countries and the economic priorities of the country. Between poor countries under dictatorship and democracy the difference is negligible. We cannot say that democracy guarantees development, but we can expect it not to lag behind dictatorships."),
